<LegalPage title="Security Policy - Doer" description="Report Doer security issues to Aryan Gupta and understand connected-tool protections." heading="Doer Security Policy" lede="Please report security issues privately so they can be investigated and fixed." effectiveDate="2026-10-04" lastUpdated="2026-10-05" sections={sections}>
  <section id="reporting"><h2>Reporting an issue</h2><p>Send vulnerability reports to <a href="mailto:aryangupta4feb@gmail.com">aryangupta4feb@gmail.com</a>, operated by Aryan Gupta. Include the affected version, a description of the impact, and reproduction steps. Remove credentials and personal data from examples. Please avoid public disclosure of an exploitable issue while we investigate. Response and resolution times depend on severity and available resources; there is no paid bounty program.</p></section>
  <section id="scope"><h2>Scope and responsible research</h2><p>This policy covers Doer software and <a href="https://doer.lagaryan.click">doer.lagaryan.click</a>. It does not authorize testing Google, Microsoft, T3 Tools, AI providers, or other people's Doer installations. Test with your own accounts and disposable local data. Do not access another person's information, disrupt services, send unwanted email, or keep data you do not own.</p></section>
  <section id="protections"><h2>Connected-tool protections</h2><p>Gmail uses Google OAuth with one-use sign-in state and PKCE. Gmail credentials are encrypted at rest, and desktop key storage uses operating-system protection. Gmail sign-in is disabled if secure storage is unavailable. Every connector email requires a one-time review of its exact contents; approvals cannot grant permission for future email. Disconnect revokes Google access before deleting stored credentials.</p><p>Local document edits are constrained to the selected Space, checked against the inspected version, written through a temporary file, and accompanied by an original backup. These safeguards do not protect against a compromised operating system or malicious software already running with your account's privileges.</p></section>
  <section id="responsibilities"><h2>Protecting your computer</h2><p>Install updates, lock and encrypt your device, keep backups, and use only providers and paired devices you trust. A provider with broad computer or file permissions can access information outside the connected-tool boundaries. Doer is not an isolation boundary for untrusted software. Do not expose your local server to other people unless you intend to share its tasks and enabled tools.</p><p>Some desktop releases are unsigned. Check that downloads come from the official <a href="https://github.com/LAG-4/doer/releases">Doer releases</a>. OAuth client configuration included in a desktop application can be extracted; it is not a substitute for Google user consent, PKCE, and protected user tokens.</p></section>
  <section id="contact"><h2>Contact</h2><p>For security and support, contact <a href="mailto:aryangupta4feb@gmail.com">aryangupta4feb@gmail.com</a>. If Gmail access is no longer wanted, disconnect in Doer or revoke it through <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections">Google account connections</a>.</p></section>
</LegalPage>
